---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const articles = [
  {
    title: 'I can\'t let AI near my real, sensitive work',
    subtitle: 'Why al-Nizam can be trusted with PII, HIPAA, PCI, and the work that makes the difference between safe and exposed',
    date: '2026-06-10',
    href: '/leadership/trust-comes-from-structure/',
    series: 'Introducing al-Nizam — Boundaries',
  },
  {
    title: 'AI forgets everything the moment I close the tab',
    subtitle: 'How al-Nizam keeps continuity that doesn\'t depend on the AI tool remembering',
    date: '2026-06-10',
    href: '/leadership/memory-and-pipeline-in-practice/',
    series: 'Introducing al-Nizam — Amnesia',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Leadership — al-Nizam"
  description="Long-form pieces examining the disciplines al-Nizam has evolved. Memory, governance, continuity, trust, and the operating layer between operator and AI."
  theme="light"
>
  <article>
    <h1>Leadership</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      Long-form pieces examining the disciplines al-Nizam has evolved. Each piece
      takes a problem the world is already struggling with, shows how most people
      cope, then shows the structural answer al-Nizam evolved.
    </p>

    <p>
      The series accrues into a worldview rather than a feature tour. Pieces can
      be read in any order. Sequencing recommendation lives in each piece's
      header.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <h2>Articles</h2>

    <ul class="article-list">
      {articles.map((article) => (
        <li>
          <h3><a href={article.href}>{article.title}</a></h3>
          <p class="meta">{article.series} · {article.date}</p>
          <p>{article.subtitle}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <p class="lead">
      <em>More pieces in this series ship as the framework's discipline evolves.
      Each piece is built to be read alone or as part of the accumulating
      worldview. Subscribe via <a href="/leadership/rss.xml">RSS</a> to follow
      the cadence.</em>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
